  "body": "# IDC Skills Forge 2.0.3\n\nForge 50 hardening release: signed content integrity, externally anchored anti-rollback freshness, expanded dangerous-Git and zero-egress scanner gauntlets, and cross-platform release verification.\n\n## Release evidence\n\n- Public merge: `26b9285c1fe11a3ef875a34ff30faa0275eddf24`\n- Signed tree: `0ca09971998a058ca80c05fbfde4ca4d1178fdf8`\n- Reviewed signed candidate: `0545afad89a9f21dd7c0837f7b0c3be3f505db72`\n- Manifest sequence: `1`\n- Manifest SHA-256: `beb78e369c93eb077136c88821776481b9c074e72d1bda63231c4296639375b1`\n- Freshness index sequence: `1`\n- Freshness index SHA-256: `3819c3aef522bd157c10df06f02fb9e52831d8fc3ec1657877ccd2db92b9f1d9`\n- Index publication commit: `b96035df279849d1539fce051a917f7519f9effb`\n- Signing fingerprint: `SHA256:LBkF4ekX2Z1XQ08gjjExnku92wAgmyFA04YJqPiczbA`\n\nThe manifest and freshness index use domain-separated OpenSSH signatures. Clean staging and public clones both returned `readyToRun=true` with `5/5+freshness`; full reacceptance passed `50/50`, all tests, four native targets, and 50 snapshot ZIPs.\n\nCI run 32509316016 passed on macOS, Ubuntu, and Windows for the exact signed candidate. Staging PR #4 was merged without rewriting the signed tree.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Only the independently installed freshness launcher can emit `readyToRun=true`; the in-tree verifier emits content readiness only.\n- Manifest v3 binds the full tracked release closure, file modes, verifier, launcher, signing anchors, and 50 skills.\n- The expiring signed index binds the exact public merge and rejects rollback, replay, equivocation, and source drift.\n- Private staged execution, pinned runtime hashes, clean consumer environments, and protected checkpointing reduce post-verification substitution risk.\n- The dangerous-Git guard and static egress scanner gained substantially expanded adversarial Bash 3.2 matrices while retaining documented advisory boundaries.\n\nThe attached manifest/signature and index/signature pairs are the release authority artifacts. Repository changelog wording that calls 2.0.3 a candidate records the signed pre-promotion state; this GitHub release is the external post-sign publication receipt.\n"
